---
import MemoLayout from '../layouts/MemoLayout.astro';
import { links } from '../data/links';
---
<MemoLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Colton Bearden: IT administrator and builder, working in Microsoft 365, Azure and identity, running a six-machine homelab, and keeping AI on hardware in plain view."
  kicker="About"
>
  <p>
    I'm a Windows-and-Linux administrator and builder who likes
    infrastructure that proves itself.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>My background is Global Administrator work across Microsoft 365, Azure and identity.</li>
    <li>I run a homelab of six machines joined by a private mesh network.</li>
    <li>I keep global site-packages lean and virtual environments in one place, managed by uv.</li>
    <li>I write commits in the Conventional Commits format, with subjects of fifty characters or fewer.</li>
    <li>I think AI is best run where it can be observed: on my own hardware, doing legible work.</li>
    <li>I build this site in public; its source is on <a href="https://github.com/coltonbearden/coltonbearden.com">GitHub</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Write-ups live under <a href="/blog/">Notes</a>, and the machines and
    tools behind them are listed under <a href="/uses/">Uses</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Elsewhere: {links.map((l, i) => (
      <>{i > 0 && ', '}<a href={l.href} rel="me">{l.label}</a></>
    ))}.
  </p>
</MemoLayout>
